@startuml affordability_sources
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' affordability_sources — v28.4 (§J.2): where "the work" comes from.
' Read top-down: one question, two sources, one honest admission. The
' multiplier box is the §J.2 payoff: history turned into a coefficient.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

rectangle "**affordability(task)**\n« how much is still to do? »" as q #E8F0EC

rectangle "**estimate exists?**\n(own — or the SUM of its\npieces' estimates)" as est #FFFFFF

rectangle "**ESTIMATE PATH** (v28.4)\noutstanding =\nestimate × **personal rate** − tracked" as epath #E8F0EC
rectangle "**PROXY PATH** (v28.0, kept)\noutstanding =\nblocks planned − tracked" as ppath #FFFFFF
rectangle "**UNKNOWN**\nno estimate AND no blocks —\n« I can't tell », said out loud" as unknown #FDF3F2

rectangle "**personalMultiplier()**\nmedian of actual ÷ estimate\nover finished, tracked,\nestimated tasks\n(1.0 under 3 samples;\nclamped 0.5–3.0;\nderived, never stored)" as mult #E8F0EC

q --> est
est --> epath : yes
est --> ppath : no, but blocks\nwere planned
est --> unknown : no, and none\never were
mult -right-> epath : the rate

legend bottom
  One verdict pipeline, two sizing sources: the user's **estimate** (scaled by
  their own measured rate) outranks the planned-blocks **proxy**; Unknown has
  shrunk to the case where BOTH are absent. Format unchanged — everything
  here is derived.
endlegend
@enduml
